{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars","id":315103,"title":"Social Physicality Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-18T00:23:32-08:00","id":315103,"title":"Social Physicality Lunars","content":"So with the Lunar themes being more defined by physicality, how do you think this can affect mental stats? Physical stats are no brainers, social stats are actually not that hard either. You've got somebody who either shapeshifts to disappear into a crowd or looking at you with the most warm, trustworthy face you've ever seen in your life or having an otherworldly beauty that puts people into a suggestible trance.<br /> <br /> The mental stats are a lot harder though, does anyone have any ideas on how you could do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T00:33:27-08:00","id":315127,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can actually think of is Mangaverse Reed Richards in the Eva parody, wherein he literally stretches the neurons of his brain to make more connections so that he becomes temporarily smarter. This is, of course, completely ridiculous, but it's the only thing I can think of wherein one becomes &quot;physically smarter&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T00:38:43-08:00","id":315130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315127#post315127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I can actually think of is Mangaverse Reed Richards in the Eva parody, wherein he literally stretches the neurons of his brain to make more connections so that he becomes temporarily smarter. This is, of course, completely ridiculous, but it's the only thing I can think of wherein one becomes &amp;quot;physically smarter&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I thought about stuff like that and it just doesn't seem to work, no more lizard hind brain stuff please. Awareness I can actually see some physical stuff for, but wits less so and nothing for int.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:23:53-08:00","id":315173,"title":"","content":"well - wits is about quick reactions and quick thinking<br /> <br /> I like the idea of fluffing up lunar charm expressions as temporary minor mutations. Maybe extra sensitive skin/hair to feel movement in the air - or eyes that briefly become animal-ish to account for heightened sensitivity.<br /> <br /> also, IIRC, there is a lunar int charm that says that you literally grow more brain temporarily to help solve a problem - so... ya","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:01:17-08:00","id":315199,"title":"","content":"Where would intuition or instinct fit in? Wits or Intelligence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:35:15-08:00","id":315206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315199#post315199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would intuition or instinct fit in? Wits or Intelligence?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of both I'd say.<br /> <br /> I guess Intelligence would mostly involve changing the way the Lunar thinks, or interprets. So he suddenly sees the world through much older, more wisened eyes, or there's a voice in his head that's telling him about things he didn't really see, or interprets them in ways he normally couldn't. That second one taps more into the idea of madness, but I am just throwing things out there, crazy people tend to not think like normal people, after all.<br /> <br /> The problem with Lunars is that their inspirations (barbarians and mythical monsters) don't really have a lot of 'thinking' related powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:55:36-08:00","id":315210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315206#post315206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of both I'd say.<br /> <br /> I guess Intelligence would mostly involve changing the way the Lunar thinks, or interprets. So he suddenly sees the world through much older, more wisened eyes, or there's a voice in his head that's telling him about things he didn't really see, or interprets them in ways he normally couldn't. That second one taps more into the idea of madness, but I am just throwing things out there, crazy people tend to not think like normal people, after all.<br /> <br /> The problem with Lunars is that their inspirations (barbarians and mythical monsters) don't really have a lot of 'thinking' related powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well take Conan for example. Many times in Howard's stories he would outwit more civilized or intelligent people, because he had a pragmatic cleverness and intuition that was gained by his lifestyle and upbringing as a barbarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:09:56-08:00","id":315215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315210#post315210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well take Conan for example. Many times in Howard's stories he would outwit more civilized or intelligent people, because he had a pragmatic cleverness and intuition that was gained by his lifestyle and upbringing as a barbarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but doesn't that give them a lot of overlap with Solars? I mean, pragmatic cleverness is not unique to barbarians, Batman has it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:19:06-08:00","id":315220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315215#post315215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but doesn't that give them a lot of overlap with Solars? I mean, pragmatic cleverness is not unique to barbarians, Batman has it too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Batman's focus is in his abilities, not his self. He's an amazing martial artist, and the world's greatest detective. These a skills you learn. Conan's intuition and cleverness isn't something that's taught. It's part of him, he was born with it..<br /> <br /> You will see Solar charms that help being a detective by working off of Investigation. You won't see Solar charms help being a detective by working off intuition. There is bound to be overlap, that's just a truth of the game, but how each splat approaches the overlap is different. A Solar with Investigation charms will find all the clues and connect the dots. A Lunar will take a look and follow the gut, knowing she's right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:25:58-08:00","id":315222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315220#post315220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman's focus is in his abilities, not his self. He's an amazing martial artist, and the world's greatest detective. These a skills you learn. Conan's intuition and cleverness isn't something that's taught. It's part of him, he was born with it..<br /> <br /> You will see Solar charms that help being a detective by working off of Investigation. You won't see Solar charms help being a detective by working off intuition. There is bound to be overlap, that's just a truth of the game, but how each splat approaches the overlap is different. A Solar with Investigation charms will find all the clues and connect the dots. A Lunar will take a look and follow the gut, knowing she's right.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very true. Makes me wonder how far you can stretch that concept though. It also feels like a bit of a disconnect within their powerset. I mean, if you have abilities like 'dodge attacks by turning bodyparts into swarms of snakes' or 'fill your body with the great strength of an elephant', having a gut feeling doesn't really feel like it belongs in there, just my impression though, kind of depends on the presentation.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I recently read Scion, and there's a powerset in there called Jotunsblut (Giant's blood) where the Scion can let mortal followers drink his blood in order to be granted some of his strength. Since I don't really see Lunars training people, would this be a viable ability for Lunars to have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:31:15-08:00","id":315224,"title":"","content":"I think one could go with areas in which one engages in physical action with a certain form of precision or result, like examining something for the particular point in a wall where a strike will cause the structure to crumble.<br /> <br /> Maybe also transitioning through various forms of psychedelic or lunatic state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:57:00-08:00","id":315233,"title":"","content":"To be fair, John talked about the physicality in response to a question about illusions, saying they're not creating things outside themselves, because their powers are part of their body.<br /> So we may be over-interpreting things. That doesn't preclude powers about their mind (and I mean mind, not physical brain).<br /> Lunars could well still have Counting the Elephant's Wrinkles (which goes with what John was saying about the mythic connotations of animals) without needing to fluff it as &quot;your brain mutates so that you regenerate neurons&quot; or something.<br /> But, stuff isn't external to you. So presumably no walking on moonbeams or magically infusing the local area with fertility (though that'd be a fine spell you could learn).<br /> But stuff like being able to see spirits by having magic eyes, finding things using echolocation with your magic ears, never forgetting with your magic brain, making intuitive leaps with your magic mind, is probably fine without actually needing to, say, grow some sort of special brain.<br /> I'm not sure however, it opens up much new areas that weren't there before, and as a No Moon player I'd really like a lot more than the tiny amount of charms there was before (as I've said on another thread, Perception is fine, but Int and Wits are not).<br /> I thought perhaps they could bring out the moon-related themes to give Lunars, say, a tree of Wits charms about insanity (which is associated with the Moon in most cultures) but that's not really related to the internal nature of their charms. Well, defensive insanity as a social defence might be, but not inflicting madness on others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T04:04:51-08:00","id":315237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315224#post315224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe also transitioning through various forms of psychedelic or lunatic state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the Moon is so associated with insanity, I'd like to see this.<br /> <br /> Honestly, since No Moons are so deprived of themes to build charms on compared to Full and Changing Moons, I'll basically take any theme that's not ridiculous if it inspires the devs to write a bunch of cool charms.<br /> I don't really care if some of the themes are odd, as long as I get to buy some Wits charms that aren't just Dex copy-paste or Elsewhere-related. About a quarter of the Wits charms are just upgrades to your elsewhere den.<br /> Hmmm... that makes me wonder if Lunars will still have Elsewhere dens, it being entirely external to them. Which really means they need some more themes for Wits.<br /> It's also just occurred to me that, IIRC, the devs said there'll be no more Wyld charms. That's about a third of the Intelligence charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T04:15:24-08:00","id":315242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315237#post315237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Moon is so associated with insanity, I'd like to see this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And Lunars specifically... all that talk of rage...<br /> <br /> I think people should also remember that John has mentioned how Lunars shape themselves <u>and perceptions of themselves</u>. That latter one probably has a lot of potential.<br /> <br /> I wonder, would a Charm to make people intuit that you have a certain expertise whether you do or not, would that be Manipulation or Intelligence/Wits?<br /> <br /> Although on that note, now I'm thinking of an Intelligence Charm (or sequence of them) that lets a Lunar stumble through some technical task in which they don't really have any training or experience, and coming through with something functional. Not necessarily the same result as somebody who knew what they were doing, certainly something that looks rough edged and inexpert, but it still gets the job done.<br /> <br /> Lunars might not have Sail Charms, and might not have their particular specific take on the image of a sailor, but they might still have their weird kind of Intelligence that helps keep them from being useless while on a boat.<br /> <br /> Even if that might ultimately amount to strategic and artful ways of crashing it into things. :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T05:15:38-08:00","id":315280,"title":"","content":"I find the idea that a Lunar's power is strictly of the self strange. The moon wasn't mad, but it caused lunacy in others. Is there a possibility of having a wider design base than what was suggested? I mean, changing how other perceive them could range from tricking their target, to literally instilling a different thing onto their perceptions. The first is a very passive method, the other an overt method. Is there room for both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T05:48:28-08:00","id":315298,"title":"","content":"Okay, some shape shifting inspired mental powers, many tapping into the Moon's themes of madness!<br /> <br /> 1. Social defense charm-Rewrite your brain to induce synaesthesia, rendering your enemies (or allies!) attempts to convince you of thing merely an unpleasant odor or flicker of swirling color or the brush of silk on your skin. Fun for role playing!<br /> 2. Mad Science! Alter your brain chemistry to eliminate the need for sleep as long as you're working on your current project! Gain a derangement/whatever 3E uses for insanity of obsession towards said project!<br /> 3. Lunacy! Convert one of your intimacies into a harder-to-oppose madness! Your love for your daughter becomes creepy and overbearing and paranoid,but nobody can talk you into eating her!<br /> 4. Super smarts! Turns out that if you shut off the parts of your brain that are working on unnecessary stuff (read: your intimacies, mostly, and digestion, and breathing, and your heartbeat, etc), you can devote the extra processing power to genius works of induction! A Lunar can roll her eyes up in her head,hold her breath, suffer a surely-minor epileptic fit, and then predict the immediate future like a sci-fi military supercomputer doing combat simulations. Mentat, go!<br /> 5. Speaking of Wits, turns out converting your nerves to living silver speeds up your thought processes and reaction time enough for you to &quot;stop time&quot; briefly.&quot; Doesn't let you move around or anything, but it can give you a moment to get your bearings or take mental actions. Think the Robert Downey Jr Sherlock Holmes fight scenes or clue connecting bits. Higher levels might let you do sorcery stuff with less ritual casting time or do fancy &quot;actually moving around while everyone is frozen as a flash of moonlight&quot; shenanigans.<br /> 6. People would be a lot smarter without all those distractions! Blind and deafen yourself to go into a meditative fugue state to perform projects entirely in your mind! This is Int, not Wits, by the way. Make blueprints for your manse, do months of research on your new spell in mere hours, internalize the contents of the library you just read so you can write it out later (burn the original so those meddling snake bloods can't get at it), write your great novel in thirty minutes in your head, etc.<br /> 7 Mental compartmentalization! Divide your super-brain into two personalities! One of 'em handles everyday stuff while the other designs artifacts and does research projects in the background...and takes over the controls if you get mind-controlled to fuck up whoever did it! Alternately, split your brain up and let your patsy-personality get seduced/mind-controlled/tortured and then take back over once the time is right! Bonus points if you have to choose how you divide your intimacies between your split personalities when you're not merged.<br /> 8. I'm running low on time, so, um...go look at Mega Int and Mega Wits from Aberrant? Lotsa good ideas there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T06:25:00-08:00","id":315344,"title":"","content":"A lot of the Mega Int stuff was super science though. But there are a few bits there.<br /> I do actually like the split personalities a lot, in terms of the occasional trope in shows or books where the genius character mind-controls or mind-wipes themselves to get whatever they need or escape their foes, or whatever, then gets their memories back later. Could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T06:58:50-08:00","id":315352,"title":"","content":"Does one really have to go out of their way to explain mental charms in a place of physicality? Your mind is in your body, you know? It's part of it. Upgrading the mind is upgrading the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T07:05:31-08:00","id":315363,"title":"","content":"Stereotypically intelligence based superpowers are a good start for this. I feel there's a bit of thematic risk here, but things like Psi powers and cobbling together one-of-a kind devices out of scraps are the sorts of things generally attributed to those with superhuman minds. Mind reading (or accurately modeling someone elses's mental OS in you own more advanced machine to predict their responses in something like mindreadin), prophecy, mind control, mental blasts, etc. The superhuman mind has some tropes to it that might not work for Lunars...but these sorts of Supers genre characters can be a good jumping off point. Maybe telepathy is out of theme...but sending messages across the world by visiting your friends's dreams seems Lunar enough. A good desk inning can make most powers fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T07:38:49-08:00","id":315378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315130#post315130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I thought about stuff like that and it just doesn't seem to work, no more lizard hind brain stuff please. Awareness I can actually see some physical stuff for, but wits less so and nothing for int.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, no more even mentioning triune brain BS as something that should be on the table, I agree.<br /> <br /> Given that sensory organs are one of the few outward signs to work with for mental faculties, they may be pulling triple duty an awful lot of the time. On the few occasions when they aren't, it may be a function displayed by tattoos or stigmata markings, or the body twisted into an ascetic posture made exaggerated by shapeshifting, perhaps even going beyond mandala tattoos and into makming the body a mandala. Kundalini is also described as an instinctive force, and is likened to current, so it might also be possible to pilfer the Alchemical &quot;I'm giving off sparks!&quot; aesthetic, only without the machinery and circuits involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T07:45:02-08:00","id":315383,"title":"","content":"You brought this on yourselves. <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vWz9VN40nCA\" data-code=\"vWz9VN40nCA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vWz9VN40nCA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T07:54:21-08:00","id":315386,"title":"","content":"Perception is a matter of increasing either the amount off neurons associated with, say, the olfactory bulb, or introducing aspects like the tapetum lucidum for night vision (or octagons to the rod-cone range in Pratchett books to see magic). Intelligence is a matter of temporary dendrite growth, increased NT production, faster transition from short-term to long-term memory, transdimensional brain folding (the Beyond in the brain, so to speak), and higher conductivity of the neural coating. Wits might revolve around NT (dopamine and ACh especially), fast-twitch muscle development, increased short-term memory spacing, and better pattern-recognition.<br /> <br /> I honestly see Lunars deliberately invoking 'fight-flight-stall' via adrenaline, with further enhancement costing 1hl to replicate the surge naturally being caused by actually being injured, a viable option for a battle-length surprise anticipater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T09:27:13-08:00","id":315476,"title":"","content":"I see there's a growing concept that physicality means scientifically quantified biological functions, which I don't believe is the direction Exalted is going in, let alone Lunars. Is it possible to do physicality without the biological details?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T09:55:44-08:00","id":315488,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Godjaw;n315476Is it possible to do physicality without the biological details?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I honestly see using the biological details as solid ground for Lunars. The fuundamental notion of shapeshifting is complete control of the self, knowledge of one's own strengths and weaknesses. I honestly wished people had to go through things like Rubber stretchy Arms and muscle density manipulation before getting into the animal forms and war forms. Like hands down, you cannot turn into a bird until you learn how to manipulate the density of your bones to make yourself lighter. So saying Lunars aren't going to use biology is, literally, killing all my enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> That being said, I suppose we could use more glowing moonlight mind-orbs for Intelligence-as-storage, or piercing moonlight x-ray vision eyeballs up in here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T10:51:47-08:00","id":315522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315488#post315488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly see using the biological details as solid ground for Lunars. The fuundamental notion of shapeshifting is complete control of the self, knowledge of one's own strengths and weaknesses. I honestly wished people had to go through things like Rubber stretchy Arms and muscle density manipulation before getting into the animal forms and war forms. Like hands down, you cannot turn into a bird until you learn how to manipulate the density of your bones to make yourself lighter. So saying Lunars aren't going to use biology is, literally, killing all my enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> That being said, I suppose we could use more glowing moonlight mind-orbs for Intelligence-as-storage, or piercing moonlight x-ray vision eyeballs up in here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thing is that's not very mythic at all, far too scientific with it's notions. Devs have already stated that stretchy arms and the like are not the direction they're taking Lunars. They have mythic god-bodies, not superpowers. The more you use biological nomenclature, the less it becomes mythic. Sharpening your senses to the hidden flows of essence is not the same as manipulating your sensory systems like ocular and olfactory. <br /> <br /> So how would one do interesting physicality without getting into the biological nitty gritty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:10:50-08:00","id":315530,"title":"","content":"If they don't have things like stretchy arms but they have to be physical, I honestly have no idea what the devs could possibly be planning for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:29:57-08:00","id":315542,"title":"","content":"There are probably ways to do stretchy arms that aren't in the style of Mister Fantastic.<br /> <br /> Holden has certainly idealised an image that includes the notion of extended limbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:38:09-08:00","id":315555,"title":"","content":"Threads like this are why I'm content to wait without speculation.<br /> <br /> I'm not a neuroscientist, nor am I any other medical specialist. However, I've read <i>The Journey to the West</i> cover to cover, and striking one's name from the rolls of death followed by gorging oneself on Phoenix livers and Lao Zi's pills and the Celestial peaches feels a lot more appropriate to Exalted than physically turning off the genetic code that causes aging as a way of becoming immortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-18-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:11:31-08:00","id":315598,"title":"","content":"Lunars will have insane sense Charms through the roof* (its one of the obvious ways that are part of pre-scientific culture that animals are known to be often better than us), but I think other mental attributes are harder. Particularly intelligence, mental speed, cunning and intuition through Wits are easier.<br /> <br /> *and I could see a lot of their sense Charms helping them get information and solve problems other splats might not get through Awareness Charms - Why do I need a brain? I just know the answer through my enhanced senses anyway - I feel it through the wind, I feel what you think in the way you move, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:27:57-08:00","id":315619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315383#post315383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You brought this on yourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lA61zFPl78I\" data-code=\"lA61zFPl78I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lA61zFPl78I/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T13:05:34-08:00","id":315650,"title":"","content":"It's pretty easy to do this without getting all scientific about it and killing the magic.<br /> <br /> You don't turn other tissue into nervous tissue for more brain power, you turn your nerves into moonsilver rivers flowing between your chakras. You don't do fight-or-flight bursts of adrenaline, you fill your spirit with the essence and alertness of a wild beast. You don't stretch your arms out to reach your opponents, you flash towards them to close the distance with the speed of thunder and the strength of a falling mountain.<br /> <br /> Lunars turning sci-fi is one of the worst things that could happen to them, I suspect, and I suspect that's one of the reasons the Devs are leaning away from Pistol Shrimp Ignites the Sun Atemi and other biologically-inspired Lunar charm ideas. Lunars oughta feel magic, rather than feel like sci-fi shapeshifters shoehorned into a magic setting. A Lunar changing shape isn't like Beastboy or Clayface changing shape, she doesn't need to explain her powers scientifically: she just &quot;becomes&quot; what she's turning into. It's spiritual or shamanistic or magical, not a quantifiable physical effect. Turning into a wolf should feel like a skinchanger donning a wolf's skin to turn into one-you shouldn't be concerned with crap like adapting to an unfamiliar body plan or suddenly different senses or which nipple your nipple piercing ends up on!<br /> <br /> But sci-fi CAN give us a solid pile of &quot;supergenius powers&quot; and effects, some of which can be re-skinned to fit Lunar themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T13:25:54-08:00","id":315674,"title":"","content":"The thing is that's exactly what Silver Solar powers are, and why I'm very uncomfortable with the emphasis on physicality. &quot;Supergenius powers&quot; are exaggerations of human talents, which therefore fall under Solar material, so it seems likely to just give us Silver Solars again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:12:16-08:00","id":315716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315173#post315173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well - wits is about quick reactions and quick thinking</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it wants to be.<br /> <br /> The problem with &quot;quick thinking&quot; is it really has never been made applicable to any normal rolls in Exalted except maybe speeding up crafting, which has always been Intelligence.<br /> <br /> In any case this reveal about increasing physicality has left me uncomfortable and slightly concerned about Lunars, because Full Moons were never the Caste with the most problems being competitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315242#post315242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people should also remember that John has mentioned how Lunars shape themselves <u>and perceptions of themselves</u>. That latter one probably has a lot of potential.<br /> <br /> I wonder, would a Charm to make people intuit that you have a certain expertise whether you do or not, would that be Manipulation or Intelligence/Wits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's reassuring actually. As I've said, my favorite Lunar Charms are those that are &quot;look like an everyman/look like the person your target most wants to see/look like the person your target most expects to see.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:19:14-08:00","id":315718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315716#post315716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with &quot;quick thinking&quot; is it really has never been made applicable to any normal rolls in Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not like people cared about Join Battle or anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:49:43-08:00","id":315733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315718#post315718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's not like people cared about Join Battle or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If JB is the only relevant thing that Wits does, I say phase out Wits. A whole Attribute needs to have more relevance than one fucking type of roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T16:08:48-08:00","id":315747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315733#post315733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If JB is the only relevant thing that Wits does, I say phase out Wits. A whole Attribute needs to have more relevance than one fucking type of roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still better than Appearance not being rolled at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T16:13:58-08:00","id":315752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315747#post315747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still better than Appearance not being rolled at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not equivalent. Appearance was the second 2e god-stat because of MDV modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T16:52:21-08:00","id":315766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315215#post315215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but doesn't that give them a lot of overlap with Solars? I mean, pragmatic cleverness is not unique to barbarians, Batman has it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>If overlap with Solars is grounds for withholding a power from a splat, nobody's gonna get to do ANYTHING.<br /> <br /> E:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315752#post315752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not equivalent. Appearance was the second 2e god-stat because of MDV modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could really see paring it down to six Attributes. You could merge Strength and Stamina such that one stat governs both damage dealt and damage mitigated, in the same way that Dexterity affects both accuracy and evasion, turn Appearance into a Merit rather than a stat that's either too broad or too narrow, and shuffle some of Wits' functionality into Manipulation (it always struck me as odd that your ability to think on your feet had zero overlap with fast-talk and misdirection) and the rest into Perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","user":"Thesaurasaurus","date":". 11-18-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:16:03-08:00","id":315776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315733#post315733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If JB is the only relevant thing that Wits does, I say phase out Wits. A whole Attribute needs to have more relevance than one fucking type of roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the only thing Wits did, I'd call for it. In fact, more or less <i>every combat roll</i> that uses a mental Attribute is keyed off of Wits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:30:56-08:00","id":315783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315776#post315776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, more or less <i>every combat roll</i> that uses a mental Attribute is keyed off of Wits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, what else are you thinking of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:54:40-08:00","id":315792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315783#post315783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what else are you thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saving yourself from a fall.<br /> Foiling pickpockets.<br /> Recalling academic knowledge on the fly.<br /> Tampering with evidence.<br /> Operating a First Age device.<br /> Evading trackers.<br /> Stabilizing a dying person on a battlefield, or, indeed, stanching a wound in general.<br /> Remaining on a panicked mount.<br /> Not being surprised for a surprise attack.<br /> Not being surprised <i>again</i> when someone tries to re-establish surprise.<br /> Resisting being disarmed.<br /> Join Battle.<br /> Join War.<br /> Join Debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:47:18-08:00","id":315820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315792#post315792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saving yourself from a fall.<br /> Foiling pickpockets.<br /> Recalling academic knowledge on the fly.<br /> Tampering with evidence.<br /> Operating a First Age device.<br /> Evading trackers.<br /> Stabilizing a dying person on a battlefield, or, indeed, stanching a wound in general.<br /> Remaining on a panicked mount.<br /> Not being surprised for a surprise attack.<br /> Not being surprised <i>again</i> when someone tries to re-establish surprise.<br /> Resisting being disarmed.<br /> Join Battle.<br /> Join War.<br /> Join Debate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.chzbgr.com/maxW500/1625864448/h756A73C0/\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Now help me think of ways to pretend Appearance doesn't affect MDV, and is instead a rolled Attribute, and circumstances when Appearance is rolled.<br /> That way, I can play a Changing Moon and feel like having an Excellency that doesn't affect a set cap of mental influence matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:53:10-08:00","id":315822,"title":"","content":"Join X was a given and is apparently the majority of what Wits hangs its hat on in terms of everyday usefulness.<br /> <br /> Noticing pickpockets and surprise being tied to Wits instead of Perception? The hell? Yes noticing surprise is good...commonly delegated to a surprise negator tho.<br /> <br /> Yeah I have seen most of those rolls come up a grand total of Never times. Or STs never saw that list and defaulted to different Attributes, like remembering on the fly or operating a FA device being Intelligence. Which, I'll admit is not a real indictment of the system itself, except maybe in being overly granular in specific rolls in a way that unfortunately reminds me of Shadowrun.<br /> <br /> In any case, do those compare in terms of useful scope to all attack rolls, potentially all social change-your-mind rolls, generally noticing things, soak/resisting poison/disease, etc.? No. If anything that list proves Wits is a kitchen sink that tries to be involved in a lot with no unifying theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315820#post315820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now help me think of ways to pretend Appearance doesn't affect MDV, and is instead a rolled Attribute, and circumstances when Appearance is rolled.<br /> That way, I can play a Changing Moon and feel like having an Excellency that doesn't affect a set cap of mental influence matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatically affecting a defense value and negating successes is a much better deal than the chance of rolling.<br /> <br /> Seduction makes sense as rolled Appearance + Presence. I think WoD uses that pool at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T19:43:52-08:00","id":315835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315822#post315822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I have seen most of those rolls come up a grand total of Never times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, your games sound boring.<br /> <br /> Brasstreader, whatever your image is, I'm not seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-18-2014, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T19:51:06-08:00","id":315837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315835#post315835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, your games sound boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically, in a game where Charms have historically removed the need to roll certain things and just allow success with the use of the Charm, a common result is using Charms even when you don't strictly &quot;need&quot; to, because they're guaranteed and not subject to the vagaries of chance.<br /> <br /> But whatever guy thanks for the insult it really added a lot to this talk about mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T21:09:16-08:00","id":315879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315822#post315822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seduction makes sense as rolled Appearance + Presence. I think WoD uses that pool at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic WoD used a system cribbed from the James Bond RPG. First, it was Appearance + Subterfuge (for the Opening Line). Next up was Wits + Subterfuge (flirty Banter) Then it was Charisma + Empathy (Conversation). The target numbers for each were based on the mental Attributes of the target (Wits, Intelligence, and Perception, in that order for the above).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T02:22:29-08:00","id":316095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=315716#post315716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said, my favorite Lunar Charms are those that are &quot;look like an everyman/look like the person your target most wants to see/look like the person your target most expects to see.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally like to see it take a form of &quot;You look exactly the same as always, the target just gets an impression that they <i>should</i> be happy to see you; even if you're a complete stranger, they have a sense of ease and familiarity (possibly with them seeing real or imagined similarities between you and the person they <i>would</i> have most liked to turn up at that point. At its strongest, the person even starts to wonder if you might be a person they know in some kind of disguise, even if that should be impossible.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Lunar Scarecrow from Wicked...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that's exactly what Silver Solar powers are</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels to me as though the biggest problem with Silver Solar Charms was that they were written in exactly the same way as Solar Charms, and arranged in categories of function that basically made them feel as though they were Ability Charms in all but prerequisite.<br /> <br /> I would say that, if a holistic approach is taken to Charm cascades (namely that not every power has to be following the same conceit, so long as they're arranged in complementary structures that ultimately create a distinct playstyle), they're written in a notably different manner from Solar ones (which we've already seen to be rather intricate and comprehensive), and don't try to stretch applications of Attributes into every space whether they fit a Lunar aesthetic or not, then having some Charms with minimal embellishments won't really be so bad.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters, but they're also divinely inspired madpeople, and that divinity can flow through them to create some effects more than mechanistic body additions might. One should just remember the characteristics of that divinity they're inspired by.<br /> <br /> And one of the characteristics of Luna is her strange, huge intellect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T10:31:32-08:00","id":316391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316095#post316095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that, if a holistic approach is taken to Charm cascades (namely that not every power has to be following the same conceit, so long as they're arranged in complementary structures that ultimately create a distinct playstyle), they're written in a notably different manner from Solar ones (which we've already seen to be rather intricate and comprehensive), and don't try to stretch applications of Attributes into every space whether they fit a Lunar aesthetic or not, then having some Charms with minimal embellishments won't really be so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>This misses the point. I have yet to see a concept for a new Lunar Intelligence Charm that would not fall directly under something a Solar should also get. This is problematic because while sure, some of the Lunar Intelligence Charms should probably just be Solar Intelligence-related Charms with a coat of paint, right now the <i>entire theoretical Lunar Intelligence Charm space</i> is exactly the same as the Solar Intelligence-related space except with some of the abilities stripped out for not fitting Lunars.<br /> <br /> It's easy to design Charms for Full Moons that make them as good or better at what they do than Solars and in a different way from Solars. Full Moons are not the ones who need help here. I haven't seen you, or anyone else, put forward a hypothetical No Moon Charm that didn't also fit a Twilight, aside from Reed Richards stretchy brain. Which is not a concept that one founds an entire Charmset on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:54:15-08:00","id":316428,"title":"","content":"That's not true. In this thread people have suggested lunacy and dreams as a good thematic base for lunar int and wits charms.<br /> <br /> Int charm, based on lunacy: <br /> Moon-mad methodology<br /> Like their patron goddess, the lunars tread intellectual paths others would avoid. This has aided Luna in his endevours and the same is true for her chosen. Whenever presented with a task that demands a roll with an int component, the lunar may (something crunchy and not overpowered here. I'm not even going to try since it's not my strong suit nor relevant to the point I'm trying to make) representing how they can reach a conclusion to a problem by unorthodox thinking. This charm earned the Lunar scholars of the past much annoyance from their solar colleagues who after much calculation would find that the answer the lunars would give would be right. The lunars would shrug and go on to claim that the meaning of life was 42 and chuckle smugly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T12:53:27-08:00","id":316453,"title":"","content":"Lunars should be able to voluntarily go insane in order to perform certain tasks or protect themselves. There should be Int charms that render the mind of the lunar impenetrable (please no perfect...) because they twisted their own mind into a maddening maze of crazy. They should be able to fragment their own personality into 20 different ones, allowing him to never sleep as they all sleep at different times; allowing him to complete calculus while fighting; allowing him to break mental control by switching (&quot;Looks like I can't leave myself alone for 10 minutes...&quot;). This is something from which I can see a whole charmset grow from, and this is the kind of charm-set which allows for character growth and identity crisis WITHOUT becoming a were-wolf or a chimera.<br /> <br /> Lunars should be able to answer to &quot;You're crazy!&quot; with something like &quot;A crazy mind is a mind <i>shattered</i> by the world. It is a <i>weak</i> mind broken by reality. I <i>fragmented, dissected</i> my mind, rearranged it in such a way that you might <i>find</i> crazy, but which is in fact <i>so much more</i> than anything you can imagine!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T13:17:47-08:00","id":316476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lunars should be able to answer to &quot;You're crazy!&quot; with something like &quot;A crazy mind is a mind <i>shattered</i> by the world. It is a <i>weak</i> mind broken by reality. I <i>fragmented, dissected</i> my mind, rearranged it in such a way that you might <i>find</i> crazy, but which is in fact <i>so much more</i> than anything you can imagine!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or with the phrase &quot;Of course, otherwise, this wouldn't work.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:40:03-08:00","id":316589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316453#post316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars should be able to voluntarily go insane in order to perform certain tasks or protect themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was already a thing with Commanded to Fly, the irony being it got worse as your natural mental defenses actually improved.<br /> <br /> I don't know that I'd want to see that concept super-expanded though. I don't think &quot;short-lived mental illness as a shield&quot; is a good Charm theme for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:47:21-08:00","id":316592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316589#post316589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was already a thing with Commanded to Fly, the irony being it got worse as your natural mental defenses actually improved.</div> </div> </div> </div>And your shapeshifting capabilities, don't forget that. Heck, it only takes one bird form to render the name of the Charm an inapplicable use of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:49:22-08:00","id":316596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316592#post316592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your shapeshifting capabilities, don't forget that. Heck, it only takes one bird form to render the name of the Charm an inapplicable use of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>ugh ugh ugh ugh ugh indeed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T16:26:00-08:00","id":316611,"title":"","content":"I get that the Moon has associations of insanity, but thinking aloud, Charm enhanced madness that is functionally superior to sanity seems easier for the Fair Folk and Infernals to wear.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time thinking of Lunars as mentally &quot;ill&quot; per se. Physically they are all about being &quot;ever strong&quot; and ever hungry, not twisted. I'd think of their minds as ultra healthy if anything? Very healthy minds which are very different, in ways that have a lot of raw &quot;animal magnetism&quot; and also in ways that are not always very nice. The kind of health that is a very beautiful fit person with more energy in their body than their skin can seem to contain smiling at you with very white, yet very sharp teeth.<br /> <br /> Some kind of altered mental states which are more to do with strangeness and heightenedness without the connotation of being ill or corrupt, yet working better anyway, seems to fit them. That whole connection to illness with paradoxical, counter intuitive functional superiority doesn't really fit with Lunars to me compared to some other splats (overlap is OK, but uniqueness is also to be celebrated and worked towards), who are more about being irrational from a human perspective and yet somehow superior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 11-19-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T21:17:25-08:00","id":316916,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of madness, a good direction for Lunar mental Charms would involve unpredictability and obfuscation (especially fitting for No Moons, whose Caste abilities they derive from). Drecain's Moon-Mad Methodology Charm is a good example of one application of supernatural lateral thinking. It seems thematically appropriate that the Lunars, whose patron is active when the world is dark and uncertain, would be best able to forge a connection with the obscure and have access to otherwise hidden knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T22:20:01-08:00","id":316947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316916#post316916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe instead of madness, a good direction for Lunar mental Charms would involve unpredictability and obfuscation (especially fitting for No Moons, whose Caste abilities they derive from). Drecain's Moon-Mad Methodology Charm is a good example of one application of supernatural lateral thinking. It seems thematically appropriate that the Lunars, whose patron is active when the world is dark and uncertain, would be best able to forge a connection with the obscure and have access to otherwise hidden knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like someone who's studied and knows a lot? Someone who is an expert scholar? Someone who is shaping up to not be very Lunar at all?<br /> <br /> The 1e process for differentiating this, which was one of the least mechanically borked Charms in the entire book, was to have Lunars go into trances and vision quests to acquire clues and such that they shouldn't have. Apparently, there was a mystic chant that No Moons taught the Lunars they tattooed that allowed them to know anything. The one above that went further and had a quest through the Lunar's interior mindscape (not the Wyld, unlike the 2e Charm that it was closest to) to determine, as noted, details that were hidden and rarefied but which were not gained by any structured means of questioning or investigation. So the physicality of the Lunar mental Charms is like Sokka on cactus juice, only when the mushroom cloud bursts up he suddenly understands the underpinnings of the Manhattan Project, or that someone has such a secret project going on that can make bombs with explosions that kick up into the mushroom-type appearance when used, or something else that involves clouds in the shape of fungal reproductive structures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-20-2014, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T02:53:35-08:00","id":317208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316947#post316947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the physicality of the Lunar mental Charms is like Sokka on cactus juice, only when the mushroom cloud bursts up he suddenly understands the underpinnings of the Manhattan Project, or that someone has such a secret project going on that can make bombs with explosions that kick up into the mushroom-type appearance when used, or something else that involves clouds in the shape of fungal reproductive structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of some imagery from Mage: the Awakening I find attractive, of questing up the length of your own spinal column.<br /> <br /> My one concern is for the possibility that that is more suitable to the Getimians; I'd need to wait to see what the full potential of the internal pattern spiders thing is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T03:00:04-08:00","id":317210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316391#post316391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen you, or anyone else, put forward a hypothetical No Moon Charm that didn't also fit a Twilight</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't put forward hypothetical Charms, I've hardly any head for mechanics.<br /> <br /> I've put forward overall themes for Charms and possibly even cascades, and sensibilities that could be produced in service of a distinct play experience, mind.<br /> <br /> No, wait... I suggested that idea of an Intelligence Charm to give off an impression of having an expertise that you don't, didn't I? In contrast to a Solar Bureaucracy Charm to make evident tha actual fact of your prowess.<br /> <br /> So... still wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T03:03:09-08:00","id":317214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=317208#post317208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one concern is for the possibility that that is more suitable to the Getimians; I'd need to wait to see what the full potential of the internal pattern spiders thing is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking off... Will the Getimians use Ability-based Charm Trees?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T08:33:07-08:00","id":317393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=317214#post317214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking off... Will the Getimians use Ability-based Charm Trees?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quoth KMFDM, &quot;What's going to happen? Nobody knows.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:51:46-08:00","id":317570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=316947#post316947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like someone who's studied and knows a lot? Someone who is an expert scholar? Someone who is shaping up to not be very Lunar at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Lateral thinking is, by definition, finding a solution through creative and indirect thought. A Lunar using Charms to enhance this would be capable if making logical leaps that have little to do with academic study. Possible examples could include:<br /> the afore-mentioned 1e Charms ( Diving the Hidden Truth, i think)<br /> uncovering forgotten knowledge<br /> uncovering knowledge others have intentionally tried to conceal<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:44:28-08:00","id":317773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=317570#post317570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. Lateral thinking is, by definition, finding a solution through creative and indirect thought. A Lunar using Charms to enhance this would be capable if making logical leaps that have little to do with academic study. Possible examples could include:<br /> the afore-mentioned 1e Charms ( Diving the Hidden Truth, i think)<br /> uncovering forgotten knowledge<br /> uncovering knowledge others have intentionally tried to conceal</div> </div> </div> </div>Lateral thinking is actually required for some &quot;conventional&quot; operations, and is still quite accessible through the capability to synthesize thought from known facts. Neither lateral thinking nor logical leaps are what Divining the Hidden Truth or Lore-Speaking Method were at all, since those were outright magical and made no attempts to hide that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T21:53:31-08:00","id":319606,"title":"","content":"On the subject of knowing stuff without Lore or conventional Investigation, some unique Lunar Intelligence Charms would be better versions of Intimate Training Recollection, Lessons in the Blood and Predator's Insight.<br /> <br /> Comb through the stolen memories of the people you ate. Or fucked. Or beat in a game of cards, if Lunars get that sort of Heart's Blood stealing ability like I hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:30:24-08:00","id":319697,"title":"","content":"If one wants to pursue the idea that Lunars are more dependent on intuition and &quot;gut-feelings&quot; than Solars, then Lunar Intelligence Charms should provide results that even the Lunar doesn't fully understand.<br /> <br /> He wants to create an artifact weapon to defeat his foe, and his supernatural intuition points him in the direction of particular ingredients... but he doesn't really know WHAT those ingredients should come together to become until he's gathered them all. So his intuition points him in the right direction, but doesn't allow him to plan ahead for the final result. Knowing that he was making an artillery piece instead of a sword would have been really handy when he'd started months and months ago.<br /> <br /> Or when he's investigating a crime, his intuition points him towards the place where he'll learn what he needs to know, but he doesn't know WHAT he's looking for there... until he manages to find it. IF he finds it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T07:23:56-08:00","id":319873,"title":"","content":"Intuition and gut feelings should probably be Wits tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T07:49:35-08:00","id":319885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=319606#post319606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of knowing stuff without Lore or conventional Investigation, some unique Lunar Intelligence Charms would be better versions of Intimate Training Recollection, Lessons in the Blood and Predator's Insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I've been speculating on Lunar charms myself and those came up as possible Intelligence charms. I'll post what I've gotten so far once the NDA clears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=319873#post319873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intuition and gut feelings should probably be Wits tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Wits will already be hax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T08:06:43-08:00","id":319891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=319885#post319885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Wits will already be hax.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome. Wits is certainly due for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:32:25-08:00","id":319943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=319873#post319873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intuition and gut feelings should probably be Wits tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of time-scales, I believe.<br /> <br /> Does the Lunar have at least an hour to think over the problem and spends at least that long thinking about it? Intelligence, the power to patiently sort through your memories and puzzle out solutions, but not necessarily to have the right answer in an instant.<br /> <br /> Is the Lunar reacting to shit happening right this very second? Wits, the power to react well under pressure, but not the endurance necessary to stick with a problem until you figure out the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:41:10-08:00","id":320333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/315103-social-physicality-lunars?p=319885#post319885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I've been speculating on Lunar charms myself and those came up as possible Intelligence charms. I'll post what I've gotten so far once the NDA clears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}